climate change activist greta toonberg  arriving at youth cop a u.n climate  change meeting in milan  a slightly reluctant celebrity although  comfortable enough to give a defiant and  dismissive speech about the failure of  politicians to tackle global warming  build back better blah blah blah green  economy blah blah blah these words will  ring in the ears of world leaders as  they gather for the next major climate  summit being held in glasgow later this  year known as cop26  and tunburg along with ugandan activist  vanessa nakate had some harsh criticism  for the country in charge  the united kingdom is the host of cop 26  in glasgow later this year but it  continues to grant new licenses to  extract oil and gas in the north sea  does that dent its moral authority in  your view i'll say that's a textbook  example of hypocrisy the uk is very good  at creating carbon accounting  um  excluding emissions and etc etc so it's  very easy at them to to make it seem  like they are taking  leadership and it's i find it very  strange that  they're like they are the ones who we  are supposed to look up to now  but they are  objectively one of the biggest climate  villains  do you think of the united kingdom as a  climate villain  i think they are because true climate  leadership  doesn't mean opening new core parlance  or funding new oil fields true climate  leadership is  prioritizing the people and the planet  over profits do you  accept that  we are  in the hands of politicians right now  and they operate in a world where they  think about what is possible not what is  perfect a report by the un showed that  the global emissions are expected to  rise by 16  compared to 2010 levels by 2030. i mean  that says it all we think that we are  moving in the right direction but the  emissions are actually still increasing  so we are not doing the right thing  whatever they are doing they are doing  it wrong have you given up on them  well i haven't given up on them because  if i give up it means communities like  mine will continue to face the worst of  the climate crisis  bound up as it is in politics and  realism cop 26 in glasgow is unlikely to  meet the high ideals of the youth  climate movement  they may not have given up but they  probably will be disappointed  hannah thomas peter sky news in milan
 

